    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0547" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg535"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Marshall to General Chang
                        Chih-chung</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-10">March 10, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am leaving for the United States tomorrow, Monday evening, March 11th, for a
                    short absence. I request that Lieutenant General Alvan C. Gillem, Jr., U. S.
                    Army be accepted as my representative on the Committee of Three and as advisor
                    to the Military Sub-Committee during the period I am absent from China.</p>
                <closer><signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
